{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794851855149,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"id":"prt_1e581db2d001DCcgBWCP1V6KBc","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e581ca35001eFBUOya0jodGN3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"8152b87bc7010179d1b2b7934c2c65a248fd2620"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794851858427,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e581e5f4001KdQk1EIj5BbYWw","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e581ca35001eFBUOya0jodGN3","type":"tool","id":"call_dc5b8b1e42d441e9b5962cfe","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md"},"output":"---\nname: sk-code-review\ndescription: \"Stack-agnostic code-review for sk-code: findings-first severity, security/correctness minimums, and surface evidence.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Write]\nversion: 1.9.18.0\nmetadata:\n  family: sk-code\n---\n\n# sk-code-review Mode - Stack-Agnostic Findings-First Review\n\nUniversal findings-first review baseline paired with `sk-code` surface standards evidence for the detected code surface.\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers\n\nUse the `sk-code-review` mode (of the sk-code family) when:\n- A user asks for code review, PR review, or merge readiness.\n- A workflow dispatches `@review` for pre-commit or gate validation.\n- A user requests security/correctness risk analysis before merge.\n- A user wants severity-ranked findings with file:line evidence.\n\n### Keyword Triggers\n\n`review`, `code review`, `pr review`, `audit`, `security review`, `request changes`, `findings`, `blocking issues`, `merge readiness`\n\n### Use Cases\n\n1. Review-only pass: findings-first output with no code edits.\n2. Gate validation: a pass or fail that follows severity for orchestrated workflows, with any score advisory only.\n3. Focused risk pass: security, concurrency, correctness, or removal-focused review.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- Feature implementation without review intent; load the surface packet (`sk-code-skilled`) that carries the implement doctrine.\n- Pure documentation editing where code behavior is not being assessed.\n- Git-only workflow tasks (branching, rebasing, commit hygiene) without code quality evaluation intent.\n- Applying review fixes after findings are accepted; load the surface packet (`sk-code-skilled`) that carries the implement doctrine.\n- Author-side quality gates before review; use `sk-code-quality`.\n- Root-cause debugging; use the surface's `workflow-debug.md` doctrine.\n- Verification evidence collection; use the surface's `workflow-verify.md` doctrine.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nThe hub bundles this mode for a code review, a pull-request review, merge readiness or a security and correctness pass over a diff.\nIts vocabulary is `review`, `code review`, `pr review`, `audit`, `security review`, `request changes`, `findings`, `blocking issues` and `merge readiness`.\nThe first resource it loads is `references/review-core.md`, the doctrine both `@review` and `@deep-review` read.\n\nReview keeps no detection of its own.\nThe quality runner's explain entry is the one resolver, and it applies the shared detection contract, [`stack-detection.md`](../shared/references/stack-detection.md) section 2.\nA surface the hub's router bundles from request words is only a candidate: it applies to the files the resolver places in it.\n\nThe rule-override algorithm it hands to the review lives in [`review-core.md`](./references/review-core.md) section 9.\nRead [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting skill-local resources; open only the matched files.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Phase 1: Scope and Baseline\n\n1. Check the two efficiency gates in section 8 before scoping anything: M-1 skips a review whose pull request is unchanged since the last one, and M-2 skips a diff below its opt-in evidence threshold unless it touches a sensitive path. A skip ends the review there, with the status line alone.\n2. Inspect the review target (`git diff`, staged diff, file list, or commit range).\n3. Load baseline standards from the `sk-code-review` mode (of the sk-code family).\n4. Resolve the rule sources for the reviewed files in one call, from the reviewed repository's root, where `<hub>` is the sk-code folder this mode was loaded from (`.skilled/skills/sk-code` in the repository that ships it):\n\n   ```bash\n   git diff --name-only --diff-filter=d <range>   # the reviewed paths that still exist\n   node <hub>/sk-code-quality/scripts/quality-gate.cjs --explain <file> [<file>...]\n   ```\n\n   Pass only paths that exist as regular files. One deleted or missing path makes the runner stop the whole call with `FILE_NOT_FOUND`, exit 3, which would drop every surface and override for the files that do exist.\n\n   - For a diff, `--diff-filter=d` leaves the deleted paths out.\n   - For a file list, drop any path that is not a regular file.\n   - List a deleted path on the `Not checked:` line when its removal matters to the review, such as a deleted test or a removed caller.\n\n   It prints one `code-quality-explain/v1` JSON document and always exits 2, because it runs nothing. Read each `files[]` entry's `surfaces`, `surface_skills` (the folder each surface loads from), `checklists` (each with its `source`, `sources` and parsed `overrides`) and the document's `config.hygiene.disabled`.\n\n   Exit 3 on that filtered list is a usage or root fault: name it on the `Not checked:` line and review those files against the baseline only. [`runner-contract.md`](../sk-code-quality/references/runner-contract.md) section 3 owns the fields.\n5. Load `sk-code` surface standards evidence for the surfaces the resolver returned. A surface the hub's router bundled from request words is a candidate, and it applies only to the files the resolver places in it: the file's `surfaces` holds its label, or one of its checklists applies to the file. A candidate that holds no reviewed file is not loaded and not named in `Surface evidence used`.\n6. With no file paths to review, nothing is resolved. The bundle keeps `sk-code-skilled` only when the working directory is inside the hub's own checkout, the same git common dir as the hub folder. Anywhere else it drops `sk-code-skilled`, because a word such as \"typescript\" says nothing about whose code it is.\n7. Read the connected code: the callers of each changed function, the functions each changed function calls, the tests that cover it, and the README or docs that describe it. Anything you could not read goes on the `Not checked:` line.\n\n### Phase 2: Surface Alignment\n\n1. Load standards from `sk-code` for the resolved surfaces only, each for the files the resolver placed in it.\n2. Apply precedence matrix:\n   - Baseline security/correctness minimums and the rest of the floor always apply.\n   - Apply the `## Rule overrides` rows of the checklists the resolver returned. Use the precedence and outcomes of [`review-core.md`](./references/review-core.md) section 8: the repository checklist, then a specific surface, then the SKILLED fallback, then the default lens.\n     A checklist whose `overrides.refused` is true contributes no row. A hygiene rule in `config.hygiene.disabled` counts as a `none` row from the repository config.\n   - Surface style/process/verification conventions win on conflicts.\n3. If precedence cannot be resolved deterministically, escalate before scoring. Two rows at the same level that disagree apply the default, go under `Conflicts` and are named in Next Steps.\n\n### Phase 3: Findings-First Analysis\n\n1. Analyze for security and correctness first.\n2. Analyze quality/performance, test adequacy, contract safety, and architecture concerns.\n3. Analyze KISS/DRY and SOLID violations (SRP/OCP/LSP/ISP/DIP) with evidence.\n4. Analyze removal opportunities with safe-now vs deferred classification.\n5. Produce findings ordered by severity (`P0`, `P1`, `P2`), numbered once across all three groups so the first `P1` finding continues after the last `P0` finding. A finding with no case is not reported.\n6. For every actionable finding, classify fix scope as `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`. If unknown, default to class/cross-consumer until a producer/consumer inventory proves instance-only.\n\n#### Reach Calibration\n\nA `P0` or `P1` finding names its reach in its `Case:` line, and a finding that cannot name one is `P2`.\nThe rule, its exceptions for validated input and for data that crosses a trust boundary, and the limit on the low-confidence escalation rule are in [`review-core.md`](./references/review-core.md) section 2.\n\n#### Numeric Severity Calibration\n\nUse numeric calibration only as reviewer context, never as the gate.\nA finding may include an optional advisory `riskScore` to communicate relative risk, and reviewers may adjust that score by `+/-2` for local context such as exploitability, blast radius, user impact, confidence, or proven containment.\nThe blocking decision still comes only from the `P0`/`P1`/`P2` severity contract.\nDo not introduce `score>=4` or any other numeric threshold as a blocker.\n\n#### Instance-Only Opt-Out\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: sk-code-review\ndescription: \"Stack-agnostic code-review for sk-code: findings-first severity, security/correctness minimums, and surface evidence.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Write]\nversion: 1.9.18.0\nmetadata:\n  family: sk-code\n---\n\n# sk-code-review Mode - Stack-Agnostic Findings-First Review\n\nUniversal findings-first review baseline paired with `sk-code` surface standards evidence for the detected code surface.\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers\n\nUse the `sk-code-review` mode (of the sk-code family) when:\n- A user asks for code review, PR review, or merge readiness.\n- A workflow dispatches `@review` for pre-commit or gate validation.\n- A user requests security/correctness risk analysis before merge.\n- A user wants severity-ranked findings with file:line evidence.\n\n### Keyword Triggers\n\n`review`, `code review`, `pr review`, `audit`, `security review`, `request changes`, `findings`, `blocking issues`, `merge readiness`\n\n### Use Cases\n\n1. Review-only pass: findings-first output with no code edits.\n2. Gate validation: a pass or fail that follows severity for orchestrated workflows, with any score advisory only.\n3. Focused risk pass: security, concurrency, correctness, or removal-focused review.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- Feature implementation without review intent; load the surface packet (`sk-code-skilled`) that carries the implement doctrine.\n- Pure documentation editing where code behavior is not being assessed.\n- Git-only workflow tasks (branching, rebasing, commit hygiene) without code quality evaluation intent.\n- Applying review fixes after findings are accepted; load the surface packet (`sk-code-skilled`) that carries the implement doctrine.\n- Author-side quality gates before review; use `sk-code-quality`.\n- Root-cause debugging; use the surface's `workflow-debug.md` doctrine.\n- Verification evidence collection; use the surface's `workflow-verify.md` doctrine.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nThe hub bundles this mode for a code review, a pull-request review, merge readiness or a security and correctness pass over a diff.\nIts vocabulary is `review`, `code review`, `pr review`, `audit`, `security review`, `request changes`, `findings`, `blocking issues` and `merge readiness`.\nThe first resource it loads is `references/review-core.md`, the doctrine both `@review` and `@deep-review` read.\n\nReview keeps no detection of its own.\nThe quality runner's explain entry is the one resolver, and it applies the shared detection contract, [`stack-detection.md`](../shared/references/stack-detection.md) section 2.\nA surface the hub's router bundles from request words is only a candidate: it applies to the files the resolver places in it.\n\nThe rule-override algorithm it hands to the review lives in [`review-core.md`](./references/review-core.md) section 9.\nRead [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting skill-local resources; open only the matched files.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Phase 1: Scope and Baseline\n\n1. Check the two efficiency gates in section 8 before scoping anything: M-1 skips a review whose pull request is unchanged since the last one, and M-2 skips a diff below its opt-in evidence threshold unless it touches a sensitive path. A skip ends the review there, with the status line alone.\n2. Inspect the review target (`git diff`, staged diff, file list, or commit range).\n3. Load baseline standards from the `sk-code-review` mode (of the sk-code family).\n4. Resolve the rule sources for the reviewed files in one call, from the reviewed repository's root, where `<hub>` is the sk-code folder this mode was loaded from (`.skilled/skills/sk-code` in the repository that ships it):\n\n   ```bash\n   git diff --name-only --diff-filter=d <range>   # the reviewed paths that still exist\n   node <hub>/sk-code-quality/scripts/quality-gate.cjs --explain <file> [<file>...]\n   ```\n\n   Pass only paths that exist as regular files. One deleted or missing path makes the runner stop the whole call with `FILE_NOT_FOUND`, exit 3, which would drop every surface and override for the files that do exist.\n\n   - For a diff, `--diff-filter=d` leaves the deleted paths out.\n   - For a file list, drop any path that is not a regular file.\n   - List a deleted path on the `Not checked:` line when its removal matters to the review, such as a deleted test or a removed caller.\n\n   It prints one `code-quality-explain/v1` JSON document and always exits 2, because it runs nothing. Read each `files[]` entry's `surfaces`, `surface_skills` (the folder each surface loads from), `checklists` (each with its `source`, `sources` and parsed `overrides`) and the document's `config.hygiene.disabled`.\n\n   Exit 3 on that filtered list is a usage or root fault: name it on the `Not checked:` line and review those files against the baseline only. [`runner-contract.md`](../sk-code-quality/references/runner-contract.md) section 3 owns the fields.\n5. Load `sk-code` surface standards evidence for the surfaces the resolver returned. A surface the hub's router bundled from request words is a candidate, and it applies only to the files the resolver places in it: the file's `surfaces` holds its label, or one of its checklists applies to the file. A candidate that holds no reviewed file is not loaded and not named in `Surface evidence used`.\n6. With no file paths to review, nothing is resolved. The bundle keeps `sk-code-skilled` only when the working directory is inside the hub's own checkout, the same git common dir as the hub folder. Anywhere else it drops `sk-code-skilled`, because a word such as \"typescript\" says nothing about whose code it is.\n7. Read the connected code: the callers of each changed function, the functions each changed function calls, the tests that cover it, and the README or docs that describe it. Anything you could not read goes on the `Not checked:` line.\n\n### Phase 2: Surface Alignment\n\n1. Load standards from `sk-code` for the resolved surfaces only, each for the files the resolver placed in it.\n2. Apply precedence matrix:\n   - Baseline security/correctness minimums and the rest of the floor always apply.\n   - Apply the `## Rule overrides` rows of the checklists the resolver returned. Use the precedence and outcomes of [`review-core.md`](./references/review-core.md) section 8: the repository checklist, then a specific surface, then the SKILLED fallback, then the default lens.\n     A checklist whose `overrides.refused` is true contributes no row. A hygiene rule in `config.hygiene.disabled` counts as a `none` row from the repository config.\n   - Surface style/process/verification conventions win on conflicts.\n3. If precedence cannot be resolved deterministically, escalate before scoring. Two rows at the same level that disagree apply the default, go under `Conflicts` and are named in Next Steps.\n\n### Phase 3: Findings-First Analysis\n\n1. Analyze for security and correctness first.\n2. Analyze quality/performance, test adequacy, contract safety, and architecture concerns.\n3. Analyze KISS/DRY and SOLID violations (SRP/OCP/LSP/ISP/DIP) with evidence.\n4. Analyze removal opportunities with safe-now vs deferred classification.\n5. Produce findings ordered by severity (`P0`, `P1`, `P2`), numbered once across all three groups so the first `P1` finding continues after the last `P0` finding. A finding with no case is not reported.\n6. For every actionable finding, classify fix scope as `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`. If unknown, default to class/cross-consumer until a producer/consumer inventory proves instance-only.\n\n#### Reach Calibration\n\nA `P0` or `P1` finding names its reach in its `Case:` line, and a finding that cannot name one is `P2`.\nThe rule, its exceptions for validated input and for data that crosses a trust boundary, and the limit on the low-confidence escalation rule are in [`review-core.md`](./references/review-core.md) section 2.\n\n#### Numeric Severity Calibration\n\nUse numeric calibration only as reviewer context, never as the gate.\nA finding may include an optional advisory `riskScore` to communicate relative risk, and reviewers may adjust that score by `+/-2` for local context such as exploitability, blast radius, user impact, confidence, or proven containment.\nThe blocking decision still comes only from the `P0`/`P1`/`P2` severity contract.\nDo not introduce `score>=4` or any other numeric threshold as a blocker.\n\n#### Instance-Only Opt-Out\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794851857909,"end":1794851858427}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794851858437,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e581e376001Cq8keBiogeouRs","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e581ca35001eFBUOya0jodGN3","type":"tool","id":"call_5166a8a7f1c042508f09ef6b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '349,380p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; echo \"=== config template ===\"; cat .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json"},"output":"  phase_init:\n    purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n    steps:\n\n      step_preflight_contract:\n        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n        verify:\n          - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n          - dry_run_normalized: \"Boolean true or false before workflow loading; absent flag resolves to false.\"\n          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n\n      step_create_directories:\n        action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n\n      step_detect_resource_map:\n        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n        classify:\n          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n        outputs:\n          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n        action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n=== config template ===\n{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 7,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewFocus\": null,\n  \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n  \"crossReference\": {\n    \"core\": [\n      \"spec_code\",\n      \"checklist_evidence\"\n    ],\n    \"overlay\": [\n      \"skill_agent\",\n      \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n      \"feature_catalog_code\",\n      \"playbook_capability\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n    \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"inputs\": [\n      \"latestJSONLDelta\",\n      \"newIterationFile\",\n      \"priorReducedState\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": [\n      \"findingsRegistry\",\n      \"dashboardMetrics\",\n      \"strategyUpdates\"\n    ],\n    \"metrics\": [\n      \"dimensionsCovered\",\n      \"findingsBySeverity\",\n      \"openFindings\",\n      \"resolvedFindings\",\n      \"convergenceScore\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n    \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n    \"manifestPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n    \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n    \"lockedFields\": [\"lineageMode\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"mode\", \"reviewDimensions\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n    \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n  }\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  phase_init:\n    purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n    steps:\n\n      step_preflight_contract:\n        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n        verify:\n          - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n          - dry_run_normalized: \"Boolean true or false before workflow loading; absent flag resolves to false.\"\n          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n\n      step_create_directories:\n        action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n\n      step_detect_resource_map:\n        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n        classify:\n          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n        outputs:\n          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n        action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n=== config template ===\n{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 7,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewFocus\": null,\n  \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n  \"crossReference\": {\n    \"core\": [\n      \"spec_code\",\n      \"checklist_evidence\"\n    ],\n    \"overlay\": [\n      \"skill_agent\",\n      \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n      \"feature_catalog_code\",\n      \"playbook_capability\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n    \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"inputs\": [\n      \"latestJSONLDelta\",\n      \"newIterationFile\",\n      \"priorReducedState\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": [\n      \"findingsRegistry\",\n      \"dashboardMetrics\",\n      \"strategyUpdates\"\n    ],\n    \"metrics\": [\n      \"dimensionsCovered\",\n      \"findingsBySeverity\",\n      \"openFindings\",\n      \"resolvedFindings\",\n      \"convergenceScore\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n    \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n    \"manifestPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n    \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n    \"lockedFields\": [\"lineageMode\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"mode\", \"reviewDimensions\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n    \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n  }\n}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '349,380p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; echo \\\"=== config template ===\\\"; cat .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794851857270,"end":1794851858437}}}}
