{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794851933064,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58300e60012bfHzOW4PcpOVR","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e5828ebe001spBjPXFBiNsieh","type":"tool","id":"call_f5446f1d6dc2448da632c737","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"git-preflight|git-hooks-check|spec-gate hook|hook mirror readme|security policy\" .skilled/skills/*/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/*/*/ROUTER.md 2>/dev/null | head -30; echo \"=== named hook readme phrases in other routers ===\"; rg -n \"readme for the .* hook|hook readme\" .skilled/skills --glob 'ROUTER.md' | grep -v \"sk-doc/ROUTER.md\" | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:129:  contributing.md\" and \"security.md\" requests. A bare \"security policy\" phrase\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:141:  folder\" requests. \"hook mirror readme\" is left out, because \"mirror\" belongs\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:23:Requests reach this skill when they name a README, a folder readme, a code-folder readme or `/create:readme`, when they ask for developer orientation on a project, skill, feature, component or source-code directory, and when they ask for a repository's install guide, contributing guide or security policy. They also arrive when they ask for the README of a hook folder, a runtime plugin or extension folder, or a runtime folder and its `SYNC.md`. `create-skill` also hands its README step here.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:36:- `security-policy-template.md` for a repository security policy.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:48:- **`readme`** fires on `readme`, `readme for`, `folder readme`, `create readme`, `write readme`, `project readme`, `skill readme`, `install guide`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md` and `sync doc for the` at weight 4. It selects the template the target names: `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package, `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`, a root-guide template for an install guide, contributing guide or security policy, `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a hook folder, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a plugin or extension folder, `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README or `SYNC.md`, and `assets/readme-template.md` for everything else. It then loads the flat markdown inventory under `references/` and `assets/`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:66:| Repository security policy | `SECURITY.md` at the repository root | `assets/security-policy-template.md` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:109:    \"readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"readme\", \"readme for\", \"folder readme\", \"create readme\", \"write readme\", \"project readme\", \"skill readme\", \"install guide\", \"contributing guide\", \"security policy\", \"sync.md\", \"sync doc for the\"]},\n=== named hook readme phrases in other routers ===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:129:  contributing.md\" and \"security.md\" requests. A bare \"security policy\" phrase\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:141:  folder\" requests. \"hook mirror readme\" is left out, because \"mirror\" belongs\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:23:Requests reach this skill when they name a README, a folder readme, a code-folder readme or `/create:readme`, when they ask for developer orientation on a project, skill, feature, component or source-code directory, and when they ask for a repository's install guide, contributing guide or security policy. They also arrive when they ask for the README of a hook folder, a runtime plugin or extension folder, or a runtime folder and its `SYNC.md`. `create-skill` also hands its README step here.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:36:- `security-policy-template.md` for a repository security policy.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:48:- **`readme`** fires on `readme`, `readme for`, `folder readme`, `create readme`, `write readme`, `project readme`, `skill readme`, `install guide`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md` and `sync doc for the` at weight 4. It selects the template the target names: `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package, `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`, a root-guide template for an install guide, contributing guide or security policy, `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a hook folder, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a plugin or extension folder, `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README or `SYNC.md`, and `assets/readme-template.md` for everything else. It then loads the flat markdown inventory under `references/` and `assets/`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:66:| Repository security policy | `SECURITY.md` at the repository root | `assets/security-policy-template.md` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:109:    \"readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"readme\", \"readme for\", \"folder readme\", \"create readme\", \"write readme\", \"project readme\", \"skill readme\", \"install guide\", \"contributing guide\", \"security policy\", \"sync.md\", \"sync doc for the\"]},\n=== named hook readme phrases in other routers ===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"git-preflight|git-hooks-check|spec-gate hook|hook mirror readme|security policy\\\" .skilled/skills/*/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/*/*/ROUTER.md 2>/dev/null | head -30; echo \\\"=== named hook readme phrases in other rou