{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794851965315,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e583434a001xmt7wOmCWUrAw2","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e5831014001L2Cw1UMAD25IO7","type":"tool","id":"call_fd275f218d4245ca940541a6","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - sk-doc routing pass eleven\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the routing-11 lineage, tracking stage-two README intent narrowing, generated intent signals and the compiled skill graph.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - routing-11\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent state for the `routing-11` lineage of review pass eleven. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\n- **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\n- **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview of the routing area for command surfacing pass eleven: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` (v2.4.13.0), `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`. The area covers phase 039's narrowing of the README intents main added to sk-doc: the git-* and spec-gate named hook phrases, the hook mirror README phrase and the bare security policy phrase were dropped, security.md was kept, the router prose states why, and the generated intent signals and compiled skill graph follow the router.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — does every intended README request still reach sk-doc and the right leaf set, and do bare git, mirror and gate prompts stay out?\n- [ ] D2 Security — does the narrowed vocabulary avoid pulling security-policy or other sensitive prompts into a doc-authoring route, and is the security leaf still reachable?\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — do graph-metadata.json and skill-graph.json carry exactly the router's declared phrases, with no stale or orphaned phrase?\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — are the prose, the machine block and the generator contract consistent enough that a future phrase edit propagates?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Reviewing the fixes area (`command-attach.ts`, doctor install assets/tests) assigned to `fixes-11`; read-only context only.\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-11.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\n- Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\n- Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n- `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n- A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: correctness of stage-two scoring, generated-artifact parity, prose-to-machine consistency\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[None yet]\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\nIteration 1: correctness and traceability. Score the changed sk-doc stage-two vocabulary against the brief's named inputs (named hook, plugins/runtime folder, SECURITY.md, bare git/mirror/gate), then compare the router's declared phrases with `graph-metadata.json` and `skill-graph.json`.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` §2 intent prose, §3 `INTENT_SIGNALS`/`RESOURCE_MAP`; `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` `intent_signals` and `intent_signals_generated`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` `.signals[\"sk-doc\"]`.\n- Behavior claims: root-guide leaves fire on `security.md`; hook-readme leaves fire on generic hook README phrases and the named shared hooks except `git-*` and `spec-gate`; runtime-plugin-readme leaves fire on plugins/extensions folder phrases; bare `git`, `mirror` and `gate` prompts no longer pull sk-doc.\n- Generation chain: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs` carries every multi-word phrase a router declares into `graph-metadata.json`; `skill-graph.json` is the advisor's compiled graph projection of the same signals.\n- Stage-two scorer: `leaf-route-replay.cjs` scores each intent once per hit keyword (intent weight for plain keywords), keeps intents within one point of the top score, then maps `RESOURCE_MAP` to leaf pairs.\n- Review risks: the generator requires a space in a phrase (`k.includes(' ')`), so a dotted token such as `security.md` cannot propagate; the branch's phrase edit may therefore have a silent half-life.\n- Out of scope: the nested `sk-create-readme` packet router and its templates; they are context only.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - sk-doc routing pass eleven\\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the routing-11 lineage, tracking stage-two README intent narrowing, generated intent signals and the compiled skill graph.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - routing-11\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent state for the `routing-11` lineage of review pass eleven. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\\n- **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\\n- **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview of the routing area for command surfacing pass eleven: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` (v2.4.13.0), `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`. The area covers phase 039's narrowing of the README intents main added to sk-doc: the git-* and spec-gate named hook phrases, the hook mirror README phrase and the bare security policy phrase were dropped, security.md was kept, the router prose states why, and the generated intent signals and compiled skill graph follow the router.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — does every intended README request still reach sk-doc and the right leaf set, and do bare git, mirror and gate prompts stay out?\\n- [ ] D2 Security — does the narrowed vocabulary avoid pulling security-policy or other sensitive prompts into a doc-authoring route, and is the security leaf still reachable?\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — do graph-metadata.json and skill-graph.json carry exactly the router's declared phrases, with no stale or orphaned phrase?\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — are the prose, the machine block and the generator contract consistent enough that a future phrase edit propagates?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Reviewing the fixes area (`command-attach.ts`, doctor install assets/tests) assigned to `fixes-11`; read-only context only.\\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-11.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\\n- Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\\n- Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\\n- `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\\n- A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: correctness of stage-two scoring, generated-artifact parity, prose-to-machine consistency\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[None yet]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\nIteration 1: correctness and traceability. Score the changed sk-doc stage-two vocabulary against the brief's named inputs (named hook, plugins/runtime folder, SECURITY.md, bare git/mirror/gate), then compare the router's declared phrases with `graph-metadata.json` and `skill-graph.json`.\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` §2 intent prose, §3 `INTENT_SIGNALS`/`RESOURCE_MAP`; `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` `intent_signals` and `intent_signals_generated`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` `.signals[\\\"sk-doc\\\"]`.\\n- Behavior claims: root-guide leaves fire on `security.md`; hook-readme leaves fire on generic hook README phrases and the named shared hooks except `git-*` and `spec-gate`; runtime-plugin-readme leaves fire on plugins/extensions folder phrases; bare `git`, `mirror` and `gate` prompts no longer pull sk-doc.\\n- Generation chain: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs` carries every multi-word phrase a router declares into `graph-metadata.json`; `skill-graph.json` is the advisor's compiled graph projection of the same signals.\\n- Stage-two scorer: `leaf-route-replay.cjs` scores each intent once per hit keyword (intent weight for plain keywords), keeps intents within one point of the top score, then maps `RESOURCE_MAP` to leaf pairs.\\n- Review risks: the generator requires a space in a phrase (`k.includes(' ')`), so a dotted token such as `security.md` cannot propagate; the branch's phrase edit may therefore have a silent half-life.\\n- Out of scope: the nested `sk-create-readme` packet router and its templates; they are context only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794851947338,"end":1794851965315}}}}
