{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852380430,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e589dcd6001HbviDdmKlXO8R1","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e589bbe6001Brkc5XEVLdA98F","type":"tool","id":"call_bc38b49f32804152a4bbb7ae","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"Create README (workflow) Router\"\ndescription: \"Sibling router for sk-create-readme: the intent signals, the resource map and the no-match checklist a reader parses first.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-create-readme router\"\n  - \"sk-create-readme routing\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.0.4.0\nrouter_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# Create README (workflow) Router\n\nThe machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the\nlink that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nRequests reach this skill when they name a README, a folder readme, a code-folder readme or `/create:readme`, when they ask for developer orientation on a project, skill, feature, component or source-code directory, and when they ask for a repository's install guide, contributing guide or security policy. They also arrive when they ask for the README of a hook folder, a runtime plugin or extension folder, or a runtime folder and its `SYNC.md`. `create-skill` also hands its README step here.\n\nIt routes to ten artifact templates under `assets/`:\n\n- `readme-template.md` for a repository front page or a general README.\n- `skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package README.\n- `readme-code-template.md` for a source-code folder.\n- `hook-readme-template.md` for a shared hook folder and its runtime adapter folders.\n- `runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a folder a runtime loads its hooks from, or a hook mirror.\n- `runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README and its `SYNC.md`.\n- `architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n- `install-template.md` for a repository install guide.\n- `contributing-template.md` for a repository contributing guide.\n- `security-policy-template.md` for a repository security policy.\n\nIt falls back to `references/README.md` and the `references/readme/` overflow group when the artifact type or folder purpose is unclear.\n\nThe router answers one question: given a request, which skill-local resources load, in what order, and\nwhat happens when nothing matches. Every path below stays inside this skill folder, and no resource other than `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`\nloads before an intent selects it.\n\n---\n\n## 2. INTENT MODEL\n\n- **`readme`** fires on `readme`, `readme for`, `folder readme`, `create readme`, `write readme`, `project readme`, `skill readme`, `install guide`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md` and `sync doc for the` at weight 4. It selects the template the target names: `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package, `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`, a root-guide template for an install guide, contributing guide or security policy, `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a hook folder, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a plugin or extension folder, `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README or `SYNC.md`, and `assets/readme-template.md` for everything else. It then loads the flat markdown inventory under `references/` and `assets/`.\n- **`code_readme`** fires on `code folder readme`, `source-code folder readme` and `source code readme` at weight 4. It selects `assets/readme-code-template.md` and loads the same flat inventory, with `references/readme/` carrying the extended code-folder voice and pattern detail.\n\n---\n\n## 3. MACHINE ROUTER\n\nThe one machine-readable projection of the intent model above, written as `## MACHINE ROUTER` so every\nreader finds it. This section is the last in the file, and it holds the only pseudocode.\n\nRoute by artifact type first, then by folder purpose.\n\n| Request | Output | Primary Template |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Repository front page, feature or component README | `README.md` in the target folder | `assets/readme-template.md` |\n| Skill package README | `README.md` at the skill package root | `assets/skill-readme-template.md` |\n| Repository install guide | `INSTALL.md` at the repository root | `assets/install-template.md` |\n| Repository contributing guide | `CONTRIBUTING.md` at the repository root | `assets/contributing-template.md` |\n| Repository security policy | `SECURITY.md` at the repository root | `assets/security-policy-template.md` |\n| Source-code folder README | `README.md` in the source folder | `assets/readme-code-template.md` |\n| Hook folder README | `README.md` in a hook folder or one of its runtime folders | `assets/hook-readme-template.md` |\n| Runtime plugin or extension folder README | `README.md` in a folder a runtime loads its hooks from | `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` |\n| Runtime folder README or sync manifest | `README.md` or `SYNC.md` at the top of a runtime folder | `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` |\n| Skill package architecture document | `ARCHITECTURE.md` at the skill package root | `assets/architecture-template.md` |\n\nThis packet uses simple artifact routing. It selects general README or code-folder README behavior from request intent and target-folder purpose. It does not use runtime keyed resource discovery by project, stack, mode or model. The only packet-local resource groups are `references/readme/` and `assets/`.\n\nRouter resilience rules:\n\n- Load optional markdown resources only after resolving them under this packet and confirming they exist.\n- Treat `references/README.md` as the fallback route map when artifact type or folder purpose is unclear.\n- Ask for the missing artifact type, target folder or validation expectation instead of silently loading no resources.\n- Do not add a full `references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/` runtime-key router unless this packet gains real keyed resource subdirectories.\n\nUse this README decision tree:\n\n```text\nIs this a project root?\n+-- YES: write a general README using the sections the audience needs\n`-- NO: is this a reusable component?\n    +-- YES: write a component README trimmed to API, examples, configuration and known issues\n    `-- NO: is someone likely to land here?\n        +-- YES: write a focused README with overview plus needed navigation or usage\n        `-- NO: skip README and use inline comments or parent documentation\n```\n\n### Smart Router Pseudocode\n\nFor this flat-reference packet, the canonical resilient router discovers resources at call\ntime, guards and loads only what exists, scores the two artifact intents, and returns a\ndisambiguation checklist rather than silently loading nothing:\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nRESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\", SKILL_ROOT / \"assets\")\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/README.md\"\n\n# Two output artifacts; keywords come from this packet's activation triggers.\nINTENT_MODEL = {\n    \"readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"readme\", \"readme for\", \"folder readme\", \"create readme\", \"write readme\", \"project readme\", \"skill readme\", \"install guide\", \"contributing guide\", \"security policy\", \"sync.md\", \"sync doc for the\"]},\n    \"code_readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"code folder readme\", \"source-code folder readme\", \"source code readme\"]},\n}\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm the artifact type (general README vs code README)\",\n    \"Confirm the target folder\",\n    \"Confirm the validation expectation\",\n]\n\ndef discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n    docs = []\n    for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Create README (workflow) Router\"\ndescription: \"Sibling router for sk-create-readme: the intent signals, the resource map and the no-match checklist a reader parses first.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-create-readme router\"\n  - \"sk-create-readme routing\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.0.4.0\nrouter_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# Create README (workflow) Router\n\nThe machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the\nlink that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nRequests reach this skill when they name a README, a folder readme, a code-folder readme or `/create:readme`, when they ask for developer orientation on a project, skill, feature, component or source-code directory, and when they ask for a repository's install guide, contributing guide or security policy. They also arrive when they ask for the README of a hook folder, a runtime plugin or extension folder, or a runtime folder and its `SYNC.md`. `create-skill` also hands its README step here.\n\nIt routes to ten artifact templates under `assets/`:\n\n- `readme-template.md` for a repository front page or a general README.\n- `skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package README.\n- `readme-code-template.md` for a source-code folder.\n- `hook-readme-template.md` for a shared hook folder and its runtime adapter folders.\n- `runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a folder a runtime loads its hooks from, or a hook mirror.\n- `runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README and its `SYNC.md`.\n- `architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n- `install-template.md` for a repository install guide.\n- `contributing-template.md` for a repository contributing guide.\n- `security-policy-template.md` for a repository security policy.\n\nIt falls back to `references/README.md` and the `references/readme/` overflow group when the artifact type or folder purpose is unclear.\n\nThe router answers one question: given a request, which skill-local resources load, in what order, and\nwhat happens when nothing matches. Every path below stays inside this skill folder, and no resource other than `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`\nloads before an intent selects it.\n\n---\n\n## 2. INTENT MODEL\n\n- **`readme`** fires on `readme`, `readme for`, `folder readme`, `create readme`, `write readme`, `project readme`, `skill readme`, `install guide`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md` and `sync doc for the` at weight 4. It selects the template the target names: `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package, `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`, a root-guide template for an install guide, contributing guide or security policy, `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a hook folder, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a plugin or extension folder, `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README or `SYNC.md`, and `assets/readme-template.md` for everything else. It then loads the flat markdown inventory under `references/` and `assets/`.\n- **`code_readme`** fires on `code folder readme`, `source-code folder readme` and `source code readme` at weight 4. It selects `assets/readme-code-template.md` and loads the same flat inventory, with `references/readme/` carrying the extended code-folder voice and pattern detail.\n\n---\n\n## 3. MACHINE ROUTER\n\nThe one machine-readable projection of the intent model above, written as `## MACHINE ROUTER` so every\nreader finds it. This section is the last in the file, and it holds the only pseudocode.\n\nRoute by artifact type first, then by folder purpose.\n\n| Request | Output | Primary Template |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Repository front page, feature or component README | `README.md` in the target folder | `assets/readme-template.md` |\n| Skill package README | `README.md` at the skill package root | `assets/skill-readme-template.md` |\n| Repository install guide | `INSTALL.md` at the repository root | `assets/install-template.md` |\n| Repository contributing guide | `CONTRIBUTING.md` at the repository root | `assets/contributing-template.md` |\n| Repository security policy | `SECURITY.md` at the repository root | `assets/security-policy-template.md` |\n| Source-code folder README | `README.md` in the source folder | `assets/readme-code-template.md` |\n| Hook folder README | `README.md` in a hook folder or one of its runtime folders | `assets/hook-readme-template.md` |\n| Runtime plugin or extension folder README | `README.md` in a folder a runtime loads its hooks from | `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` |\n| Runtime folder README or sync manifest | `README.md` or `SYNC.md` at the top of a runtime folder | `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` |\n| Skill package architecture document | `ARCHITECTURE.md` at the skill package root | `assets/architecture-template.md` |\n\nThis packet uses simple artifact routing. It selects general README or code-folder README behavior from request intent and target-folder purpose. It does not use runtime keyed resource discovery by project, stack, mode or model. The only packet-local resource groups are `references/readme/` and `assets/`.\n\nRouter resilience rules:\n\n- Load optional markdown resources only after resolving them under this packet and confirming they exist.\n- Treat `references/README.md` as the fallback route map when artifact type or folder purpose is unclear.\n- Ask for the missing artifact type, target folder or validation expectation instead of silently loading no resources.\n- Do not add a full `references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/` runtime-key router unless this packet gains real keyed resource subdirectories.\n\nUse this README decision tree:\n\n```text\nIs this a project root?\n+-- YES: write a general README using the sections the audience needs\n`-- NO: is this a reusable component?\n    +-- YES: write a component README trimmed to API, examples, configuration and known issues\n    `-- NO: is someone likely to land here?\n        +-- YES: write a focused README with overview plus needed navigation or usage\n        `-- NO: skip README and use inline comments or parent documentation\n```\n\n### Smart Router Pseudocode\n\nFor this flat-reference packet, the canonical resilient router discovers resources at call\ntime, guards and loads only what exists, scores the two artifact intents, and returns a\ndisambiguation checklist rather than silently loading nothing:\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nRESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\", SKILL_ROOT / \"assets\")\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/README.md\"\n\n# Two output artifacts; keywords come from this packet's activation triggers.\nINTENT_MODEL = {\n    \"readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"readme\", \"readme for\", \"folder readme\", \"create readme\", \"write readme\", \"project readme\", \"skill readme\", \"install guide\", \"contributing guide\", \"security policy\", \"sync.md\", \"sync doc for the\"]},\n    \"code_readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"code folder readme\", \"source-code folder readme\", \"source code readme\"]},\n}\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm the artifact type (general README vs code README)\",\n    \"Confirm the target folder\",\n    \"Confirm the validation expectation\",\n]\n\ndef discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n    docs = []\n    for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852379862,"end":1794852380430}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852380440,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e589d931001VfzHovDW7ixkOi","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e589bbe6001Brkc5XEVLdA98F","type":"tool","id":"call_74d39eed3ae44d49aac64991","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"create-readme\\|mode router\\|router\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/implementation-summary.md | head -20; echo \"=== tasks ===\"; grep -n \"create-readme\\|T0\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md | head -30"},"output":"59:| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modified | Intent signals regenerated from the router |\n71:Each candidate change was applied to a clean router, regenerated and measured against the five failing test files by `scratch/try-variant.sh`. Main's new intents were removed one at a time to find which moved the holdout count and the ratchet row, so no holdout row was read. The chosen variant then ran the full gate both ways, and the README probes went through the advisor CLI.\n=== tasks ===\n37:- [x] T001 [C] Record the failing tests and the before gates (`$SP/before.txt`). Verify: `SEVEN` shows 7 failed, and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print 24/44 0/35 2/44 and [160,49,21,5]. Evidence: before.txt: SEVEN 7 failed 63 passed (4 doctor-bridge-isolation, doctor-routing-slice, divergence ratchet, holdout-independent), FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], SIGNAL DRIFT sk-doc\n45:- [x] T002 Narrow the named hook README phrases (`$DOC/ROUTER.md`). Verify: the four isolation cases and slice rows doctor-control-11, 12 and 14 pass. Evidence: HOOK_README 58 to 44: the 12 git-* named phrases and the 2 spec-gate ones dropped; isolation x4 and doctor-control-11/12/14 pass (try-variant.sh no-git-named+names:spec-gate)\n46:- [x] T003 Narrow the runtime folder and hook mirror README phrases (`$DOC/ROUTER.md`, `$DOC/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md`). Verify: slice row doctor-a-10 passes. Evidence: \"hook mirror readme\" dropped from RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README (7 to 6); doctor-a-10 passes; sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md carries no advisor intent, left as is\n47:- [x] T004 Find which of main's new intents moved the holdout row and `rr-iter3-069`, reading only row ids and expected skills, and narrow it (`$DOC/ROUTER.md`). Verify: the holdout prints 49 of 63 or more and the ratchet passes. Evidence: one intent dropped at a time, counts only: SECURITY_POLICY \"security policy\" moved the holdout (48 to 49 without it), HOOK_README spec-gate names moved rr-iter3-069 (a labeled row, not holdout); SECURITY_POLICY keeps \"security.md\" only, any \"security policy\" phrase drops the holdout to 48; 69 of 69 pass\n48:- [x] T005 Regenerate the intent signals and recompile the graph (`$DOC/graph-metadata.json`, `$ADV/scripts/skill-graph.json`). After T004. Verify: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` and `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exit 0. Evidence: generate-router-intent-signals --write --hub sk-doc then --check RESULT: PASSED; skill_graph_compiler --export-json; skill-graph-freshness --strict exit 0, SIGNAL DRIFT none\n56:- [x] T006 [C] Probe README requests through the advisor CLI (`$SP/readme-probes.txt`). After T005. Verify: the session-handover hook, git-preflight hook and runtime folder README requests each top sk-doc. Evidence: readme-probes.txt: session-handover, git-preflight and spec-gate hook READMEs, runtime and plugins folder READMEs and SECURITY.md top sk-doc; git hooks, git rules, git standards top sk-git; runtime mirror drift tops command-doctor-runtime-mirrors\n57:- [x] T007 [C] Rebuild and rerun the gates both ways (`$SP/after.txt`). After T006. Verify: 0 failed with the flag unset and set, `FLOOR` unchanged, `EVAL` [160,49,21,5] or better, stored sets unchanged. Evidence: after.txt: stored sets unchanged, intent signals PASSED, graph freshness exit 0, build and typecheck exit 0, child run 2349 passed 0 failed, unset run 2348 passed 1 failed on the 60 ms native scorer latency p95 gate under review load, which passes 21/21 three times alone; FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5]\n58:- [x] T008 [C] Log the fix and the criterion 2 recheck (`../goal.md`). After T007. Verify: `packet_budget=ok`. Evidence: goal rows Phase 039, sk-doc routing repair and Criterion 2 recheck after phase 039; packet_budget=ok\n59:- [x] T009 [C] Close the phase (`implementation-summary.md`). After T008. Verify: `validate.sh $PK/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`. Evidence: implementation-summary filled, acceptance criteria all Met, spec Complete, validate --strict RESULT: PASSED\n60:- [x] T010 [C] Fix review pass ten's single-quoted command P1 (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`). Verify: the quote cases fail without the fix. Evidence: a single quote is dropped only where it opens a command name; three cases fail without it, 167 pass with it; contractions keep their apostrophe\n61:- [x] T011 [C] Fix review pass ten's doctor install P1 (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: the contract passes and fails with main's wording. Evidence: the presentation names claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe from the manifest; the stale DSH sentence is gone from the workflow; the test reads the manifest; 17/17, and 16/1 with main's text; doctor tests 1266/0\n62:- [x] T012 [C] Rerun the gates after the pass ten fixes (`$SP/after-pass-ten.txt`). Verify: 0 failed both ways. Evidence: 2353 passed 0 failed with the flag unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged; one doctor case failed only while the adviso