{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852395705,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58a1709001MWymgzwNcL3v0v","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e589e40a001iEQKwbIYsqadMk","type":"tool","id":"call_0222228cbe8643baa56eb3ac","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '45,70p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/implementation-summary.md; echo \"=== spec files-to-change lines ===\"; grep -n \"Files to Change\" -A 16 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->\n## What Was Built\n\nBare git prompts, the runtime mirror doctor and two scorer gates route as they did before the merge again. The sk-doc README intents main added had given sk-doc words that other skills own. Those phrases are now narrower, and README requests still reach their templates.\n\n### Phase 39: main-sk-doc-routing-repair\n\nYou can ask for \"git hooks\", \"git rules\" or \"git standards\" and reach sk-git again, and \"runtime mirror drift\" reaches `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. A request for a named hook's README, a runtime or plugins folder README or a `SECURITY.md` still lands on sk-doc. The compiled skill graph matches its sources again, so the strict freshness check passes.\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Action | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Modified | The `HOOK_README` intent drops the `git-*` and `spec-gate` named phrases, `RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README` drops \"hook mirror readme\", `SECURITY_POLICY` keeps \"security.md\" only, and the prose says why |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modified | Intent signals regenerated from the router |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modified | Recompiled graph |\n| `scratch/try-variant.py`, `scratch/try-variant.sh` | Created | Measure one keyword variant against the failing tests |\n| `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and its guards test | Modified | A single quote that opens a command name is dropped before the lead reading, from review pass ten |\n| Doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test | Modified | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence, from review pass ten |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-built -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n## How It Was Delivered\n\n=== spec files-to-change lines ===\n100:### Files to Change\n101-\n102-| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n103-|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n104-| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Modify | Narrow the README intent keywords |\n105-| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` | Modify | The same where the mode router repeats them |\n106-| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modify | Regenerated intent signals |\n107-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modify | Recompiled graph |\n108-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | Drop a single quote that opens a command name |\n109-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Quote cases |\n110-| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | Modify | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence |\n111-| `../goal.md` | Modify | Rows through the goal log command only |\n112-<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n113-\n114----\n115-\n116-<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->\n## What Was Built\n\nBare git prompts, the runtime mirror doctor and two scorer gates route as they did before the merge again. The sk-doc README intents main added had given sk-doc words that other skills own. Those phrases are now narrower, and README requests still reach their templates.\n\n### Phase 39: main-sk-doc-routing-repair\n\nYou can ask for \"git hooks\", \"git rules\" or \"git standards\" and reach sk-git again, and \"runtime mirror drift\" reaches `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. A request for a named hook's README, a runtime or plugins folder README or a `SECURITY.md` still lands on sk-doc. The compiled skill graph matches its sources again, so the strict freshness check passes.\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Action | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Modified | The `HOOK_README` intent drops the `git-*` and `spec-gate` named phrases, `RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README` drops \"hook mirror readme\", `SECURITY_POLICY` keeps \"security.md\" only, and the prose says why |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modified | Intent signals regenerated from the router |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modified | Recompiled graph |\n| `scratch/try-variant.py`, `scratch/try-variant.sh` | Created | Measure one keyword variant against the failing tests |\n| `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and its guards test | Modified | A single quote that opens a command name is dropped before the lead reading, from review pass ten |\n| Doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test | Modified | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence, from review pass ten |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-built -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n## How It Was Delivered\n\n=== spec files-to-change lines ===\n100:### Files to Change\n101-\n102-| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n103-|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n104-| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Modify | Narrow the README intent keywords |\n105-| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` | Modify | The same where the mode router repeats them |\n106-| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modify | Regenerated intent signals |\n107-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modify | Recompiled graph |\n108-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | Drop a single quote that opens a command name |\n109-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Quote cases |\n110-| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | Modify | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence |\n111-| `../goal.md` | Modify | Rows through the goal log command only |\n112-<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n113-\n114----\n115-\n116-<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '45,70p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/implementation-summary.md; echo \\\"=== spec files-to-change lines ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"Files to Change\\\" -A 16 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852394761,"end":1794852395705}}}}
