\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The accepted probe proves hub reach only, while two dropped phrase families now load the generic README leaves\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"traceability\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:136\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"readme-probes.txt:3 records the git-preflight README request topping sk-doc; stage two then scores only README_CREATION=12, so hook-readme-template.md does not load. 'write a hook mirror readme' scores README_CREATION=4 only after RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README dropped its phrase, so runtime-plugin-readme-template.md does not load. AC-003 asserts top=sk-doc, while spec.md:61 promises templates.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Extend the phase probe to assert the leaf pair for git-preflight and hook mirror, or narrow the purpose sentence to hub reach and record the generic fallback.\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"active\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"matrix/evidence\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"Scored every declared generic and named hook phrase with the leaf-route-replay rule; retained names still select their specific leaves, only the dropped families fall through.\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\n        \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/assets/hook-readme-template.md\\\",\\n        \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md\\\",\\n        \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The named skill-advisor hook phrase ties the skill README and hook README intents\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:219\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"'readme for the skill-advisor hook' contains the SKILL_README keyword 'readme for the skill' (ROUTER.md:215), so SKILL_README=16 and HOOK_README=16 are both within one point of the top and both leaf sets load.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Drop the named skill-advisor phrase in favor of the generic hook phrases, or require a word boundary that excludes a hyphenated name after 'skill'.\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"active\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"instance-only\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"Scored all 20 'readme for the ... hook' phrases; only skill-advisor produces a second top-score intent.\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\n        \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/assets/skill-readme-template.md\\\",\\n        \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/assets/hook-readme-template.md\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The 039 spec still lists the packet router as a file to change, but the delivered work left it untouched\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"traceability\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:105\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The Files to Change table names .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md as Modify; tasks.md:46 records 'left as is'; implementation-summary.md:57-63 omits it; git diff --name-only over the commit confirms it is not in the change; the packet router still carries 'security policy' and 'sync.md' at sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md:109.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Remove the row from the Files to Change table with the recorded reason, or make the narrowing change to the packet router.\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"active\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"matrix/evidence\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"Compared spec table, task evidence, implementation-summary table and the commit's file list; the hub router gates advisor entry, so no runtime caller reaches the packet through the dropped phrase.\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\n        \\\"039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md\\\",\\n        \\\"039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md\\\",\\n        \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"traceabilityChecks\\\": {\\n    \\\"results\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"protocolId\\\": \\\"spec_code\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n        \\\"gateClass\\\": \\\"hard\\\",\\n        \\\"applicable\\\": true,\\n        \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n          \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:218\\\",\\n          \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:219\\\",\\n          \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:220\\\",\\n          \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:100-111\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The router narrows exactly the scoped intents; the remaining mismatch is the packet-router row recorded as F003.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"protocolId\\\": \\\"checklist_evidence\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"notApplicable\\\",\\n        \\\"gateClass\\\": \\\"hard\\\",\\n        \\\"applicable\\\": false,\\n        \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n          \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/acceptance-criteria.md:56-58\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"summary\\\": \\\"A review pass over another phase's files has no packet checklist to certify; the phase acceptance rows were read as evidence.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"protocolId\\\": \\\"skill_agent\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n        \\\"gateClass\\\": \\\"overlay\\\",\\n        \\\"applicable\\\": true,\\n        \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:1-14\\\"],\\n        \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The change stays inside the sk-doc skill and its advisor projection; no agent file is tou