{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852574613,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58cc006001vpBtPzbKR2ZneT","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e58caf7b001VVP6vFx6axyW0E","type":"tool","id":"call_488acb191f8d4662a04e3096","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — does every intended README request still reach sk-doc and the right leaf set, and do bare git, mirror and gate prompts stay out?\n- [ ] D2 Security — does the narrowed vocabulary avoid pulling security-policy or other sensitive prompts into a doc-authoring route, and is the security leaf still reachable?\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — do graph-metadata.json and skill-graph.json carry exactly the router's declared phrases, with no stale or orphaned phrase?\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — are the prose, the machine block and the generator contract consistent enough that a future phrase edit propagates?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->","newString":"<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [x] D1 Correctness — iteration 1: hub reach holds; two dropped families fall to generic README leaves (F001); one retained name ties two intents (F002).\n- [ ] D2 Security — does the narrowed vocabulary avoid pulling security-policy or other sensitive prompts into a doc-authoring route, and is the security leaf still reachable?\n- [x] D3 Traceability — iteration 1: generated artifacts match all 14 sources exactly; one spec table row disagrees with the delivered files (F003).\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — are the prose, the machine block and the generator contract consistent enough that a future phrase edit propagates?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill