{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852584574,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58cec00001OVRpmXPSEbTG9z","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e58cda22001zJ94EzE7bfVFk6","type":"tool","id":"call_7309cb4459914ddc8a055d03","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"error","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the packet's own probe file (`039/scratch/readme-probes.txt`) before scoring anything: it turned a suspected SECURITY.md reach failure into a ruled-out direction and narrowed the real gap to the leaf level (iteration 1).\n- Diffing the declared phrases against both generated artifacts as sets: the 16 removed phrases are gone from both, `intent_signals_generated` has no orphans, and all 14 hubs match their source metadata byte-for-byte (iteration 1).\n- Reproducing the documented stage-two rule from `leaf-route-replay.cjs` instead of inventing a matcher: each finding names the intent scores that select the leaves (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- A first read treated \"README requests keep reaching their templates\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\n- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md"},"error":"Could not find oldString in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md. It must match exactly, including whitespace and indentation.\n\nThe closest lines in the file:\n77: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n78: \n79: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","metadata":{"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the packet's own probe file (`039/scratch/readme-probes.txt`) before scoring anything: it turned a suspected SECURITY.md reach failure into a ruled-out direction and narrowed the real gap to the leaf level (iteration 1).\\n- Diffing the declared phrases against both generated artifacts as sets: the 16 removed phrases are gone from both, `intent_signals_generated` has no orphans, and all 14 hubs match their source metadata byte-for-byte (iteration 1).\\n- Reproducing the documented stage-two rule from `leaf-route-replay.cjs` instead of inventing a matcher: each finding names the intent scores that select the leaves (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- A first read treated \\\"README requests keep reaching their templates\\\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\\n- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852580352,"end":1794852584574}}}}
