{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852598780,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58d211e0012wJewzJLMiZaez","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e58d13c8001SSmLwS7jeUKv2v","type":"tool","id":"call_95f046b389c34695855d695a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the packet's own probe file (`039/scratch/readme-probes.txt`) before scoring anything: it turned a suspected SECURITY.md reach failure into a ruled-out direction and narrowed the real gap to the leaf level (iteration 1).\n- Diffing the declared phrases against both generated artifacts as sets: the 16 removed phrases are gone from both, `intent_signals_generated` has no orphans, and all 14 hubs match their source metadata byte-for-byte (iteration 1).\n- Reproducing the documented stage-two rule from `leaf-route-replay.cjs` instead of inventing a matcher: each finding names the intent scores that select the leaves (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- A first read treated \"README requests keep reaching their templates\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\n- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -75,15 +75,18 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the packet's own probe file (`039/scratch/readme-probes.txt`) before scoring anything: it turned a suspected SECURITY.md reach failure into a ruled-out direction and narrowed the real gap to the leaf level (iteration 1).\n+- Diffing the declared phrases against both generated artifacts as sets: the 16 removed phrases are gone from both, `intent_signals_generated` has no orphans, and all 14 hubs match their source metadata byte-for-byte (iteration 1).\n+- Reproducing the documented stage-two rule from `leaf-route-replay.cjs` instead of inventing a matcher: each finding names the intent scores that select the leaves (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- A first read treated \"README requests keep reaching their templates\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\n+- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the packet's own probe file (`039/scratch/readme-probes.txt`) before scoring anything: it turned a suspected SECURITY.md reach failure into a ruled-out direction and narrowed the real gap to the leaf level (iteration 1).\\n- Diffing the declared phrases against both generated artifacts as sets: the 16 removed phrases are gone from both, `intent_signals_generated` has no orphans, and all 14 hubs match their source metadata byte-for-byte (iteration 1).\\n- Reproducing the documented stage-two rule from `leaf-route-replay.cjs` instead of inventing a matcher: each finding names the intent scores that select the leaves (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- A first read treated \\\"README requests keep reaching their templates\\\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\\n- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852593950,"end":17