 ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n68: \n69: - Reading the packet's own probe file (`039/scratch/readme-probes.txt`) before scoring anything: it turned a suspected SECURITY.md reach failure into a ruled-out direction and narrowed the real gap to the leaf level (iteration 1).\n70: - Diffing the declared phrases against both generated artifacts as sets: the 16 removed phrases are gone from both, `intent_signals_generated` has no orphans, and all 14 hubs match their source metadata byte-for-byte (iteration 1).\n71: - Reproducing the documented stage-two rule from `leaf-route-replay.cjs` instead of inventing a matcher: each finding names the intent scores that select the leaves (iteration 1).\n72: \n73: ---\n74: \n75: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n76: \n77: - A first read treated \"README requests keep reaching their templates\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\n78: - The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n83: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n84: ### A broken SECURITY.md reach path: the packet probe shows `create a SECURITY.md for this repo => sk-doc` despite `security.md` being absent from the generated signals (iteration 1). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n85: - What was tried: A broken SECURITY.md reach path: the packet probe shows `create a SECURITY.md for this repo => sk-doc` despite `security.md` being absent from the generated signals (iteration 1).\n86: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n87: - Do NOT retry: A broken SECURITY.md reach path: the packet probe shows `create a SECURITY.md for this repo => sk-doc` despite `security.md` being absent from the generated signals (iteration 1).\n88: \n89: ### A missing router changelog entry: `ROUTER.md` versions are file-local (`2.4.13.0`) while `sk-doc/changelog/` is skill-level (`v2.10.0.0`), so no changelog row is required for a router-only version bump (iteration 1). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n90: - What was tried: A missing router changelog entry: `ROUTER.md` versions are file-local (`2.4.13.0`) while `sk-doc/changelog/` is skill-level (`v2.10.0.0`), so no changelog row is required for a router-only version bump (iteration 1).\n91: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n92: - Do NOT retry: A missing router changelog entry: `ROUTER.md` versions are file-local (`2.4.13.0`) while `sk-doc/changelog/` is skill-level (`v2.10.0.0`), so no changelog row is required for a router-only version bump (iteration 1).\n93: \n94: ### Orphaned generated phrases after the 16-phrase removal: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` reports `orphans=0` (iteration 1). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n95: - What was tried: Orphaned generated phrases after the 16-phrase removal: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` reports `orphans=0` (iteration 1).\n96: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n97: - Do NOT retry: Orphaned generated phrases after the 16-phrase removal: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` reports `orphans=0` (iteration 1).\n98: \n99: ### Stale compiled graph or signal drift: `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with `SIGNAL DRIFT compiled vs disk: none` (iteration 1). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 100]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 30-99\n30: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n31: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (rem