{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852877952,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e59169c80014wnFdZnS1wQ4LR","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e5915e2b001dbBoqFwJD0Pb9q","type":"tool","id":"call_8feecb8ceb25441288f12911","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\n- A lexical-lane token overlap is necessary evidence, not a route proof: the lane weight is 0.28, so the residual-token finding had to be stated as a latent ambiguity instead of a current misroute (iteration 2).\n- The prose's \"git / hooks / gate\" sentence cannot be verified as one claim: two of the three words are gone and the third survives through a hook that was not in the removal set (iteration 2).","oldString":"- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -78,8 +78,10 @@\n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - A first read treated \"README requests keep reaching their templates\" as a hub-level claim; the acceptance criterion only asserts `top=sk-doc`, so the template-level gap needed the leaf scorer to surface (iteration 1).\n - The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\n+- A lexical-lane token overlap is necessary evidence, not a route proof: the lane weight is 0.28, so the residual-token finding had to be stated as a latent ambiguity instead of a current misroute (iteration 2).\n+- The prose's \"git / hooks / gate\" sentence cannot be verified as one claim: two of the three words are gone and the third survives through a hook that was not in the removal set (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\\n- A lexical-lane token overlap is necessary evidence, not a route proof: the lane weight is 0.28, so the residual-token finding had to be stated as a latent ambiguity instead of a current misroute (iteration 2).\\n- The prose's \\\"git / hooks / gate\\\" sentence cannot be verified as one claim: two of the three words are gone and the third survives through a hook that was not in the removal set (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"- The generator's `--check` cannot see a dotted phrase because it only carries phrases containing a space, so it reported `missing=0` while `security.md` was absent from the signals; the packet probe, not the gate, settled that reach still holds (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852874696,"end":1794852877952}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852877980,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5917280001xEiynzy6im8l7h","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e5915e2b001dbBoqFwJD0Pb9q","type":"tool","id":"call_a7a8cee0b81c427b98887901","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"NEXT FOCUS\" -A 6 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md; grep -n \"CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\" -A 14 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"128:## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n129-- Dimension: `security`, `maintainability`. - Focus area: the token footprint the retained named hook phrases still seed into the advisor's lexical lane, and whether the prose's stated reason for the git-* removal holds for the words it names. - Reason: iteration 1 covered correctness and traceability; the retained `env-secret-guard`, `subagent-dispatch-guard`, `decision-capture` and `session-handover` names still carry other hubs' vocabulary, which is the mechanism the change cites for the phrases it removed. - Rotation status: first pass for both dimensions. - Productive carry-forward: exact phrase-set diff plus the documented stage-two scorer; a token-level reproduction of the lexical lane. - Required evidence: tokenize the committed sk-doc signal bag with the scorer's rule, quote the lexical lane weight, and name a concrete prompt per collision. - Recovery note: none. Review verdict: PASS\n130-\n131-<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n132-## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n133-\n134-### Bounded Context Snapshot\n145:## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n146-<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n147-[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n148-\n149-| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n150