{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794853246905,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5968366001ZsywTL3rVyM6wm","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d916ffe3W1SLL4OkhFuu6","messageID":"msg_1e5967401001dWS49KqW4v5dM9","type":"tool","id":"call_b8e760292cf84553be7072dc","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - routing-11\n\nReview of the sk-doc routing area for command-surfacing pass eleven, lineage `routing-11`.\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Review scope: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`\n- Diff range: `6d50afe6f39..2f3f893c153`\n- Session: `fanout-routing-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Iterations: 3 of 8; stop reason `converged` (`all_dimensions_clean`)\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- Overall verdict: **PASS**\n- hasAdvisories: **true**\n- P0/P1/P2 counts: **0 / 0 / 5**, the counts the verdict used\n- Review scope summary: three changed files covering phase 039's narrowing of the README intents main added to sk-doc. The `git-*` and `spec-gate` named hook phrases, the `hook mirror readme` phrase and the bare `security policy` phrase were dropped; `security.md` was kept; the router prose says why; the generated intent signals and the compiled skill graph were regenerated.\n- Operator review focus: Review pass eleven. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-11.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\n- Self-check outcomes: no P0 or P1 existed, so the adversarial self-check had nothing to adjudicate; the five P2 advisories were re-verified in iteration 3.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Every named README request in the phase probe still tops sk-doc: the session-handover hook, git-preflight hook, spec-gate hook, runtime folder, plugins folder and `SECURITY.md`.\n- Bare `git hooks`, `git rules`, `git standards` reach sk-git, and `runtime mirror drift` reaches `command-doctor-runtime-mirrors`.\n- `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc` prints `RESULT: PASSED` (exit 0), and `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with no signal drift, ghost or missing node.\n- The compiled `skill-graph.json` signal arrays equal their on-disk `graph-metadata.json` sources for all 14 hubs, and `.signals[\"sk-doc\"]` equals the regenerated `intent_signals` exactly.\n\nWhat the advisories qualify:\n\n- The phase probe proves the hub top, not the template. A README request for the git-preflight hook or for a hook mirror folder now loads the generic README template rather than the hook or runtime-plugin template.\n- One retained named hook phrase (`skill-advisor`) ties the skill README and hook README intents, so two templates load.\n- More than `git` and `gate` survives: `hooks` remains via `codex-global-hooks-check`, and the other named hooks still seed env/secret, session/handover, decision/capture and dispatch/subagent tokens into sk-doc's lexical lane.\n- The 039 spec's Files to Change table still lists `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md`, but the delivered phase deliberately left it untouched.\n- The generator's carry rule and its `--check` gate share a blind spot for dotted phrases, so a change that relies on `security.md` or `sync.md` alone cannot be verified by the gate.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this verdict. The review is PASS with five advisory P2s; no P0 or P1 blocks merge. The advisories can be scheduled as a small follow-up packet.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"activeFindings\": {\n    \"P0\": 0,\n    \"P1\": 0,\n    \"P2\": 5\n  },\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AW-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Leaf-selection accuracy for the dropped phrase families\",\n      \"findings\": [\"F001\", \"F002\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AW-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Phase bookkeeping for the packet router row\",\n      \"findings\": [\"F003\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AW-3\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Vocabulary footprint and generation-gate coverage\",\n      \"findings\": [\"F004\", \"F005\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Correct or remove the 039 Files to Change row for sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md, with the reason tasks.md already records.\",\n    \"State whether a README request for a dropped named hook or a hook mirror folder intentionally falls back to the generic README template.\",\n    \"Reword the hooks rationale to the words actually removed, or remove the remaining cross-domain hook names.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add a leaf-level probe for the git-preflight and hook-mirror README requests to the phase evidence.\",\n    \"Teach generate-router-intent-signals.cjs to carry dotted filename phrases, or add a gate case for an intent with zero carryable phrases.\",\n    \"Decide whether the skill-advisor named hook phrase stays, given its tie with the skill README intent.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\n    \"matrix/evidence\",\n    \"instance-only\",\n    \"class-of-bug\"\n  ],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md\",\n    \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json\",\n    \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | File:line | Disposition |\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|-----------|-------------|\n| F001 | P2 | traceability | The accepted probe proves hub reach only, while two dropped phrase families now load the generic README leaves | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:136` | active |\n| F002 | P2 | correctness | The named skill-advisor hook phrase ties the skill README and hook README intents | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:219` | active |\n| F003 | P2 | traceability | The 039 spec still lists `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` as a file to change, but the delivered work deliberately left it untouched | `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:105` | active |\n| F004 | P2 | security | The narrowing removes the git and gate words but leaves the same cross-hub token class from the other named hooks | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:219` | active |\n| F005 | P2 | maintainability | The generator's carry rule and its `--check` gate share a blind spot for dotted phrases | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs:57` | active |\n\n### F001 - Leaf-level fallback for the dropped phrase families\n\n- Evidence: `readme-probes.txt:3` proves the git-preflight README request tops sk-doc. Stage two scores only `README_CREATION=12`, so `hook-readme-template.md` does not load. `write a hook mirror readme` scores `README_CREATION=4` only and does not load `runtime-plugin-readme-template.md`.\n- Impact: the author reaches sk-doc but starts from the generic README template.\n- Fix: extend the phase probe to assert the leaf pair, or state the generic fallback as intended.\n\n### F002 - skill-advisor named hook phrase ties two intents\n\n- Evidence: `readme for the skill-advisor hook` contains `readme for the skill` (`ROUTER.md:215`), so `SKILL_README=16` and `HOOK_README=16`; both leaf sets load.\n- Impact: two templates load where one artifact is requested, costing tokens and steering the wrong template.\n- Fix: drop the named phrase, or require a boundary that excludes a hyphenated name after `skill`.\n\n### F003 - Spec table disagrees with the delivered files\n\n- Evidence: `spec.md:105` lists `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` as Modify; `tasks.md:46` records it left as is; `implementation-summary.md:57-63` omits it; the commit does not touch it.\n- Impact: the phase's scope record overstates what changed; no runtime caller is affected because the hub router gates entry.\n- Fix: remove the row with the recorded reason, or make the change.\n\n### F004 - Residual cross-hub token class\n\n- Evidence: the committed signal bag loses `git` and `gate` but keeps `hooks` via `codex-global-hooks-check` (`graph-metadata.json:358-359`); the retained names also inject `env`, `secret`, `session`, `handover`, `decision`, `capture`, `dispatch`, `subagent`, `advisor`, `freshness`, `overlay`, `completion` and `quality`. The probe still routes `git hooks` to sk-git.\n- Impact: latent lexical ambiguity; the lexical lane's weight is 0.28 and no probe shows a present misroute.\n- Fix: reword the prose and either drop the remaining cross-domain names or restrict them to the full README phrase.\n\n### F005 - Dotted-phrase gate blind spot\n\n- Evidence: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs:57` keeps only phrases containing a space; `security.md` and `sync.md` are outside the carried set, and `--check` reports `missing=0` while `SECURITY_POLICY` declares `security.md` as its only keyword.\n- Impact: a future edit can rely on a dotted phrase and pass the gate while the advisor vocabulary lacks the intent. Reach currently holds through other lanes (probe line 7).\n- Fix: carry dotted filename phrases, or flag an intent with zero carryable phrases.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n### P0 Workstreams\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Workstreams\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Advisories\n\n1. **AW-1 - Leaf-selection accuracy (F001, F002).** Update the phase probe to assert the leaf pair for the git-preflight and hook-mirror requests, and decide the skill-advisor tie. No production behavior change is needed for the hub-top requirement.\n2. **AW-2 - Phase bookkeeping (F003).** Reconcile the 039 Files to Change table with the task record. This is a spec-doc edit, not a code edit.\n3. **AW-3 - Vocabulary footprint and gate coverage (F004, F005).** Reword the hooks rationale and extend the signal generator or its gate to cover dotted phrases. Both are follow-ups that keep the current routing behavior.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The 039 packet should say plainly that the git-* and spec-gate hook README requests reach sk-doc through the generic README intent, not the hook template, if that is the accepted trade.\n- The purpose sentence \"README requests keep reaching their templates\" should be scoped to the hub top, or the acceptance evidence should gain a leaf-level row.\n- The `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` row should be removed from the Files to Change table or the file should be changed; the current task note is a valid reason to do the former.\n- The generator contract should state which dotted filenames are carried and which are not, or the writer should carry them.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- T1: Add `git-preflight` and `hook mirror` README probes to the routing playbook, asserting the `HOOK_README` and `RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README` leaf pairs.\n- T2: Decide the skill-advisor named phrase: keep it and bound the `skill` keyword, or rely on the generic hook phrases.\n- T3: Extend `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs` to carry filename-shaped tokens, with a unit case for `security.md` and `sync.md`.\n- T4: Reword `ROUTER.md:136-137` to \"git and gate\" only, or name the remaining cross-domain hook words explicitly.\n- T5: Reconcile the 039 Files to Change table with `tasks.md:46`.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence | Drift |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | `ROUTER.md:218-220`; 039 `spec.md:100-111` | F003 only |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | 039 `acceptance-criteria.md:56-58` | none |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | `ROUTER.md:1-14` | none |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | no agent file in the diff | none |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs:124-195`; `skill-graph.json:1` | F005 |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | `readme-probes.txt:2-11` | no playbook run |\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt for this review target. The review target is the phase parent; the reviewed child packet `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair` carries its own acceptance rows, all `Met` (`acceptance-criteria.md:56-58`), and the advisory rule does not change the verdict.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- A routing playbook scenario run for the dropped-phrase leaf behavior.\n- A decision on whether the remaining cross-domain named hook phrases should be narrowed the same way as the git-* set.\n- A changelog row for the router version bump, if the repository later adopts per-router changelogs; the current convention is skill-level only.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0; failed pivots: 0; audited overrides: 0.\n- Swept: correctness of stage-two scoring (iteration 1), security and maintainability of the token footprint (iteration 2).\n- Selected directions: exact phrase-set parity, the packet probe, the documented stage-two scorer, and the scorer's token rule.\n- Remaining frontier: none. All four dimensions are covered and all six traceability protocols have a final status.\n- This map records breadth only; it does not alter the verdict or the finding registry.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record).*\n\nThe analysis performed: three iterations over three changed files; exact set comparisons across 381 declared phrases and 345 committed signals; a 14-hub signal parity check; a token intersection across the 13 other hubs; the committed advisor probe file; and the generator's carry filter. Holdout corpora were not opened; the holdout gate was read by count only.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence Summary\n\n- Stop reason: `converged`, decision `STOP`, detail `all_dimensions_clean`.\n- Iteration ratios: 1.0, 0.4, 0.0; threshold 0.10.\n- Gates: convergence, dimension coverage, P0 resolution, evidence density, hotspot saturation, claim adjudication, fix-completeness replay, candidate coverage and graphless fallback all passed at the stop.\n- Graph at the stop: 9 dimension/file nodes from the seed, 54 iteration nodes and 90 edges across three upserts; no rejected edge or self-loop.\n\n### Coverage Summary\n\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability - all covered.\n- Protocols: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` notApplicable, `skill_agent` pass, `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable, `feature_catalog_code` partial, `playbook_capability` partial.\n- Files reviewed: the three changed files, the generator and replay scripts, the scorer's text/lexical/lane files, and the 039 packet's spec, acceptance criteria, tasks, implementation summary and probe file.\n\n### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- Stale compiled graph: `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with no signal drift.\n- Orphaned generated phrases: `--check` reports `orphans=0`.\n- Broken SECURITY.md reach: the packet probe tops sk-doc.\n- Missing router changelog: the router version is file-local; the changelog is skill-level.\n- Present misroute from residual cross-hub tokens: no probe shows sk-doc beating the owning hub; the lexical lane carries 0.28.\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/leaf-route-replay.cjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lane-registry.ts`\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md`\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/acceptance-criteria.md`\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md`\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/implementation-summary.md`\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/scratch/readme-probes.txt`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` (context only)\n\n### Closeout\n\n- Verdict: PASS; hasAdvisories: true; release readiness: converged.\n- No P0 or P1 is active; no required quality gate is failing.\n- The advisory list is the five P2 findings above; none changes the release decision.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report - routing-11\\n\\nReview of the sk-doc routing area for command-surfacing pass eleven, lineage `routing-11`.\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Review scope: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`\\n- Diff range: `6d50afe6f39..2f3f893c153`\\n- Session: `fanout-routing-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Iterations: 3 of 8; stop reason `converged` (`all_dimensions_clean`)\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- Overall verdict: **PASS**\\n- hasAdvisories: **true**\\n- P0/P1/P2 counts: **0 / 0 / 5**, the counts the verdict used\\n- Review scope summary: three changed files covering phase 039's narrowing of the README intents main added to sk-doc. The `git-*` and `spec-gate` named hook phrases, the `hook mirror readme` phrase and the bare `security policy` phrase were dropped; `security.md` was kept; the router prose says why; the generated intent signals and the compiled skill graph were regenerated.\\n- Operator review focus: Review pass eleven. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-11.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\\n- Self-check outcomes: no P0 or P1 existed, so the adversarial self-check had nothing to adjudicate; the five P2 advisories were re-verified in iteration 3.\\n\\nWhat holds:\\n\\n- Every named README request in the phase probe still tops sk-doc: the session-handover hook, git-preflight hook, spec-gate hook, runtime folder, plugins folder and `SECURITY.md`.\\n- Bare `git hooks`, `git rules`, `git standards` reach sk-git, and `runtime mirror drift` reaches `command-doctor-runtime-mirrors`.\\n- `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc` prints `RESULT: PASSED` (exit 0), and `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with no signal drift, ghost or missing node.\\n- The compiled `skill-graph.json` signal arrays equal their on-disk `graph-metadata.json` sources for all 14 hubs, and `.signals[\\\"sk-doc\\\"]` equals the regenerated `intent_signals` exactly.\\n\\nWhat the advisories qualify:\\n\\n- The phase probe proves the hub top, not the template. A README request for the git-preflight hook or for a hook mirror folder now loads the generic README template rather than the hook or runtime-plugin template.\\n- One retained named hook phrase (`skill-advisor`) ties the skill README and hook README intents, so two templates load.\\n- More than `git` and `gate` survives: `hooks` remains via `codex-global-hooks-check`, and the other named hooks still seed env/secret, session/handover, decision/capture and dispatch/subagent tokens into sk-doc's lexical lane.\\n- The 039 spec's Files to Change table still lists `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md`, but the delivered phase deliberately left it untouched.\\n- The generator's carry rule and its `--check` gate share a blind spot for dotted phrases, so a change that relies on `security.md` or `sync.md` alone cannot be verified by the gate.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this verdict. The review is PASS with five advisory P2s; no P0 or P1 blocks merge. The advisories can be scheduled as a small follow-up packet.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": {\\n    \\\"P0\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P1\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P2\\\": 5\\n  },\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AW-1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Leaf-selection accuracy for the dropped phrase families\\\",\\n      \\\"findings\\\": [\\\"F001\\\", \\\"F002\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AW-2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Phase bookkeeping for the packet router row\\\",\\n      \\\"findings\\\": [\\\"F003\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AW-3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Vocabulary footprint and generation-gate coverage\\\",\\n      \\\"findings\\\": [\\\"F004\\\", \\\"F005\\\"]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Correct or remove the 039 Files to Change row for sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md, with the reason tasks.md already records.\\\",\\n    \\\"State whether a README request for a dropped named hook or a hook mirror folder intentionally falls back to the generic README template.\\\",\\n    \\\"Reword the hooks rationale to the words actually removed, or remove the remaining cross-domain hook names.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add a leaf-level probe for the git-preflight and hook-mirror README requests to the phase evidence.\\\",\\n    \\\"Teach generate-router-intent-signals.cjs to carry dotted filename phrases, or add a gate case for an intent with zero carryable phrases.\\\",\\n    \\\"Decide whether the skill-advisor named hook phrase stays, given its tie with the skill README intent.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\n    \\\"matrix/evidence\\\",\\n    \\\"instance-only\\\",\\n    \\\"class-of-bug\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs\\\",\\n    \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | File:line | Disposition |\\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|-----------|-------------|\\n| F001 | P2 | traceability | The accepted probe proves hub reach only, while two dropped phrase families now load the generic README leaves | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:136` | active |\\n| F002 | P2 | correctness | The named skill-advisor hook phrase ties the skill README and hook README intents | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:219` | active |\\n| F003 | P2 | traceability | The 039 spec still lists `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` as a file to change, but the delivered work deliberately left it untouched | `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:105` | active |\\n| F004 | P2 | security | The narrowing removes the git and gate words but leaves the same cross-hub token class from the other named hooks | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:219` | active |\\n| F005 | P2 | maintainability | The generator's carry rule and its `--check` gate share a blind spot for dotted phrases | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs:57` | active |\\n\\n### F001 - Leaf-level fallback for the dropped phrase families\\n\\n- Evidence: `readme-probes.txt:3` proves the git-preflight README request tops sk-doc. Stage two scores only `README_CREATION=12`, so `hook-readme-template.md` does not load. `write a hook mirror readme` scores `README_CREATION=4` only and does not load `runtime-plugin-readme-template.md`.\\n- Impact: the author reaches sk-doc but starts from the generic README template.\\n- Fix: extend the phase probe to assert the leaf pair, or state the generic fallback as intended.\\n\\n### F002 - skill-advisor named hook phrase ties two intents\\n\\n- Evidence: `readme for the skill-advisor hook` contains `readme for the skill` (`ROUTER.md:215`), so `SKILL_README=16` and `HOOK_README=16`; both leaf sets load.\\n- Impact: two templates load where one artifact is requested, costing tokens and steering the wrong template.\\n- Fix: drop the named phrase, or require a boundary that excludes a hyphenated name after `skill`.\\n\\n### F003 - Spec table disagrees with the delivered files\\n\\n- Evidence: `spec.md:105` lists `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` as Modify; `tasks.md:46` records it left as is; `implementation-summary.md:57-63` omits it; the commit does not touch it.\\n- Impact: the phase's scope record overstates what changed; no runtime caller is affected because the hub router gates entry.\\n- Fix: remove the row with the recorded reason, or make the change.\\n\\n### F004 - Residual cross-hub token class\\n\\n- Evidence: the committed signal bag loses `git` and `gate` but keeps `hooks` via `codex-global-hooks-check` (`graph-metadata.json:358-359`); the retained names also inject `env`, `secret`, `session`, `handover`, `decision`, `capture`, `dispatch`, `subagent`, `advisor`, `freshness`, `overlay`, `completion` and `quality`. The probe still routes `git hooks` to sk-git.\\n- Impact: latent lexical ambiguity; the lexical lane's weight is 0.28 and no probe shows a present misroute.\\n- Fix: reword the prose and either drop the remaining cross-domain names or restrict them to the full README phrase.\\n\\n### F005 - Dotted-phrase gate blind spot\\n\\n- Evidence: `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs:57` keeps only phrases containing a space; `security.md` and `sync.md` are outside the carried set, and `--check` reports `missing=0` while `SECURITY_POLICY` declares `security.md` as its only keyword.\\n- Impact: a future edit can rely on a dotted phrase and pass the gate while the advisor vocabulary lacks the intent. Reach currently holds through other lanes (probe line 7).\\n- Fix: carry dotted filename phrases, or flag an intent with zero carryable phrases.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n### P0 Workstreams\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Workstreams\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Advisories\\n\\n1. **AW-1 - Leaf-selection accuracy (F001, F002).** Update the phase probe to assert the leaf pair for the git-preflight and hook-mirror requests, and decide the skill-advisor tie. No production behavior change is needed for the hub-top requirement.\\n2. **AW-2 - Phase bookkeeping (F003).** Reconcile the 039 Files to Change table with the task record. This is a spec-doc edit, not a code edit.\\n3. **AW-3 - Vocabulary footprint and gate coverage (F004, F005).** Reword the hooks rationale and extend the signal generator or its gate to cover dotted phrases. Both are follow-ups that keep the current routing behavior.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The 039 packet should say plainly that the git-* and spec-gate hook README requests reach sk-doc through the generic README intent, not the hook template, if that is the accepted trade.\\n- The purpose sentence \\\"README requests keep reaching their templates\\\" should be scoped to the hub top, or the acceptance evidence should gain a leaf-level row.\\n- The `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` row should be removed from the Files to Change table or the file should be changed; the current task note is a valid reason to do the former.\\n- The generator contract should state which dotted filenames are carried and which are not, or the writer should carry them.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- T1: Add `git-preflight` and `hook mirror` README probes to the routing playbook, asserting the `HOOK_README` and `RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README` leaf pairs.\\n- T2: Decide the skill-advisor named phrase: keep it and bound the `skill` keyword, or rely on the generic hook phrases.\\n- T3: Extend `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs` to carry filename-shaped tokens, with a unit case for `security.md` and `sync.md`.\\n- T4: Reword `ROUTER.md:136-137` to \\\"git and gate\\\" only, or name the remaining cross-domain hook words explicitly.\\n- T5: Reconcile the 039 Files to Change table with `tasks.md:46`.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence | Drift |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | `ROUTER.md:218-220`; 039 `spec.md:100-111` | F003 only |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | 039 `acceptance-criteria.md:56-58` | none |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | `ROUTER.md:1-14` | none |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | no agent file in the diff | none |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs:124-195`; `skill-graph.json:1` | F005 |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | `readme-probes.txt:2-11` | no playbook run |\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt for this review target. The review target is the phase parent; the reviewed child packet `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair` carries its own acceptance rows, all `Met` (`acceptance-criteria.md:56-58`), and the advisory rule does not change the verdict.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- A routing playbook scenario run for the dropped-phrase leaf behavior.\\n- A decision on whether the remaining cross-domain named hook phrases should be narrowed the same way as the git-* set.\\n- A changelog row for the router version bump, if the repository later adopts per-router changelogs; the current convention is skill-level only.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0; failed pivots: 0; audited overrides: 0.\\n- Swept: correctness of stage-two scoring (iteration 1), security and maintainability of the token footprint (iteration 2).\\n- Selected directions: exact phrase-set parity, the packet probe, the documented stage-two scorer, and the scorer's token rule.\\n- Remaining frontier: none. All four dimensions are covered and all six traceability protocols have a final status.\\n- This map records breadth only; it does not alter the verdict or the finding registry.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record).*\\n\\nThe analysis performed: three iterations over three changed files; exact set comparisons across 381 declared phrases and 345 committed signals; a 14-hub signal parity check; a token intersection across the 13 other hubs; the committed advisor probe file; and the generator's carry filter. Holdout corpora were not opened; the holdout gate was read by count only.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence Summary\\n\\n- Stop reason: `converged`, decision `STOP`, detail `all_dimensions_clean`.\\n- Iteration ratios: 1.0, 0.4, 0.0; threshold 0.10.\\n- Gates: convergence, dimension coverage, P0 resolution, evidence density, hotspot saturation, claim adjudication, fix-completeness replay, candidate coverage and graphless fallback all passed at the stop.\\n- Graph at the stop: 9 dimension/file nodes from the seed, 54 iteration nodes and 90 edges across three upserts; no rejected edge or self-loop.\\n\\n### Coverage Summary\\n\\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability - all covered.\\n- Protocols: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` notApplicable, `skill_agent` pass, `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable, `feature_catalog_code` partial, `playbook_capability` partial.\\n- Files reviewed: the three changed files, the generator and replay scripts, the scorer's text/lexical/lane files, and the 039 packet's spec, acceptance criteria, tasks, implementation summary and probe file.\\n\\n### Ruled-Out Claims\\n\\n- Stale compiled graph: `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with no signal drift.\\n- Orphaned generated phrases: `--check` reports `orphans=0`.\\n- Broken SECURITY.md reach: the packet probe tops sk-doc.\\n- Missing router changelog: the router version is file-local; the changelog is skill-level.\\n- Present misroute from residual cross-hub tokens: no probe shows sk-doc beating the owning hub; the lexical lane carries 0.28.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/leaf-route-replay.cjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lane-registry.ts`\\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md`\\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/acceptance-criteria.md`\\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md`\\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/implementation-summary.md`\\n- `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/scratch/readme-probes.txt`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md` (context only)\\n\\n### Closeout\\n\\n- Verdict: PASS; hasAdvisories: true; release readiness: converged.\\n- No P0 or P1 is active; no required quality gate is failing.\\n- The advisory list is the five P2 findings above; none changes the release decision.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/routing-11/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794853208934,"end":1794853246905}}}}
